{"name":"Wet Suit","hex":"#50493c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wet suit","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of wetsuit."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wet_suit"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wet Suit (G.I. Joe)","blocks":[{"text":"Wet Suit is a fictional character from the G.I. Joe: A Real American Hero toyline, comic books and animated series. He is one of the G.I. Joe Team's Navy SEALs and debuted in 1986."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/da/Wetsuit_GIJoe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wet_Suit_(G.I._Joe)","wikidata":"Q17110130"},{"title":"Wetsuit","blocks":[{"text":"A wetsuit is a garment worn to provide thermal protection while wet. It is usually made of foamed neoprene, and is worn by surfers, divers, windsurfers, canoeists, and others engaged in water sports and other activities in or on the water. Its purpose is to provide thermal insulation and protection from abrasion, ultraviolet exposure, and stings from marine organisms. It also contributes extra buoyancy. The insulation properties of neoprene foam depend mainly on bubbles of gas enclosed within the material, which reduce its ability to conduct heat. The bubbles also give the wetsuit a low density, providing buoyancy in water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Wetsuit0806_crop.jpg/330px-Wetsuit0806_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wetsuit","wikidata":"Q13450283"},{"title":"Suit","blocks":[{"text":"A suit, also called a lounge suit, business suit, dress suit, or formal suit, is a set of clothes comprising a suit jacket and trousers of identical textiles generally worn with a collared dress shirt, necktie, and dress shoes. A skirt suit is similar, but with a matching pencil skirt instead of trousers. It is currently considered semi-formal wear or business wear in contemporary Western dress codes; however, when the suit was originally developed it was considered an informal or more casual option compared to the prevailing clothing standards of aristocrats and businessmen. The lounge suit originated in 19th-century Britain as sportswear and British country clothing, which is why it was seen as more casual than citywear at that time, with the roots of the suit coming from early modern Western Europe formal court or military clothes. After replacing the black frock coat in the early 20th century as regular daywear, a sober one-coloured suit became known as a lounge suit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Matt_Smith_on_%22Christopher_And_His_Kind%22_set.jpg/330px-Matt_Smith_on_%22Christopher_And_His_Kind%22_set.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suit","wikidata":"Q614806"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Decompression_Dive-Preparation.JPG/250px-Decompression_Dive-Preparation.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Decompression_Dive-Preparation.JPG/500px-Decompression_Dive-Preparation.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Decompression_Dive-Preparation.JPG/250px-Decompression_Dive-Preparation.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADecompression_Dive-Preparation.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Wetsuit.jpg/250px-Wetsuit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Wetsuit.jpg/500px-Wetsuit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Wetsuit.jpg/250px-Wetsuit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWetsuit.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/RNLI_Lifeguard_Jersey.JPG/120px-RNLI_Lifeguard_Jersey.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/RNLI_Lifeguard_Jersey.JPG/250px-RNLI_Lifeguard_Jersey.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/RNLI_Lifeguard_Jersey.JPG/120px-RNLI_Lifeguard_Jersey.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARNLI_Lifeguard_Jersey.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Mikebaird_-_Two_Surfing_Teens.jpg/250px-Mikebaird_-_Two_Surfing_Teens.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Mikebaird_-_Two_Surfing_Teens.jpg/500px-Mikebaird_-_Two_Surfing_Teens.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Mikebaird_-_Two_Surfing_Teens.jpg/250px-Mikebaird_-_Two_Surfing_Teens.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMikebaird_-_Two_Surfing_Teens.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/AREA_47_Rafting_Imster_Schlucht%2C_2018_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-AREA_47_Rafting_Imster_Schlucht%2C_2018_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/AREA_47_Ra